cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Expert Fleet in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Expert Fleet: a stdlib-only platform for verifiable, continuously-working expert AI agents"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Expert Fleet contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/reda-baqechame/self-learning-24.7-agent"
license: AGPL-3.0
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - autonomous agents
  - verification
  - goal contracts
  - mutation testing
  - capability packs
abstract: >-
  A file-backed, Python-stdlib-only platform for building expert AI agents
  that work continuously, prove what they did, and remember what they
  learned. Its goal system freezes acceptance tests before any planning
  (graders the worker cannot write), runs proven procedures with zero model
  calls, multiplies into parallel workers only where independence was
  declared, repairs itself only from recorded mechanical failures, and
  proves procedural competence on sealed unseen tasks. Every protection is
  mutation-tested: the feature is broken on purpose and the suite must
  notice.
